00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.160
The pages say the human body can tolerate this much jerk.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.880
If you go over the jerk, you break the vertebra.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.680
At the very end of this discussion, there were two

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.160
reasons why we shouldn't do it. They believe that if we go for

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.520
the jerk value, then the harnesses would be very large.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.040
The way it works currently in this sport, we we are in the

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.560
dark ages. There are pilots on Brazil World

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.760
Championship who still hasn't recovered from vertebral

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.840
compression. They have so serious injuries

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.520
from just a normal landing on a coroid, which would have not

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.360
been a serious issue with the previous generation harnesses.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.000
So if we know for sure that it does not work, these coroid

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.480
protectors, they do not protect the pilots.

